---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../lib/siteConfig.js";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy information for the Nixwud Consultancy website." noindex={true}>
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="container--narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lede">How information is handled when you visit or contact Nixwud Consultancy.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="container--narrow legal">
    <p class="notice"><strong>Draft for review:</strong> Replace this page with a policy reviewed for the business's legal jurisdiction and actual data-processing practices before launch.</p>
    <h2>Information you choose to provide</h2><p>If you email Nixwud Consultancy, the information in your message is used to understand and respond to your enquiry.</p>
    <h2>Website analytics</h2><p>With your permission, the website uses Google Analytics 4 to understand information such as pages visited, device type and approximate location. It may also use Microsoft Clarity to understand interactions such as clicks, scrolling and page navigation through aggregated analytics, heatmaps and masked session recordings. These tools help improve the website and are not required for it to function.</p>
    <h2>Your analytics choice</h2><p>Optional analytics are not loaded until you select <strong>Allow analytics</strong>. Your choice is stored in your browser so the website can remember it. You can review or change that choice at any time through <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer.</p>
    <h2>Downloads and browser storage</h2><p>Current resources can be used without creating an account. If email-gated resources or returning-visitor access are introduced later, this policy must be updated before that feature is enabled.</p>
    <h2>Third parties</h2><p>The website uses Sanity to provide published content. When you allow analytics, limited usage information is processed by Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity under their respective privacy terms. The website may also link to third-party websites whose privacy practices are governed by their own policies.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about privacy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
  </div></section>
</Layout>

<style>.legal a { color: var(--accent-soft); text-decoration: underline; }</style>
